"lines": [
{
"text": "Once the whole earth",
"start": 4.16,
"end": 5.26
},
{
"text": "had one word",
"start": 6.92,
"end": 7.7
},
{
"text": "one mouth",
"start": 11.081,
"end": 11.601
},
{
"text": "one breath",
"start": 13.761,
"end": 14.281
},
{
"text": "We came out of the east with the flood still in our hair",
"start": 28.542,
"end": 32.782
},
{
"text": "Found a plain in Shinar and we settled there",
"start": 35.742,
"end": 39.842
},
{
"text": "Said, \"Come, let us make bricks, let us burn them through\"",
"start": 41.683,
"end": 45.263
},
{
"text": "Brick for stone, and the pitch for glue",
"start": 45.883,
"end": 48.623
},
{
"text": "Higher, higher",
"start": 50.343,
"end": 51.383
},
{
"text": "Fire in the kiln",
"start": 51.823,
"end": 53.223
},
{
"text": "Higher, higher",
"start": 53.863,
"end": 55.043
},
{
"text": "Heaven's just a hill",
"start": 55.303,
"end": 56.903
},
{
"text": "Let us build us a city",
"start": 56.923,
"end": 58.564
},
{
"text": "Let us raise up a tower",
"start": 60.184,
"end": 63.664
},
{
"text": "With its top in the heavens",
"start": 63.724,
"end": 65.944
},
{
"text": "Let us make us a name",
"start": 66.364,
"end": 70.464
},
{
"text": "Or the wind will come scatter us",
"start": 70.844,
"end": 72.964
},
{
"text": "Over the face of the earth",
"start": 74.124,
"end": 77.185
},
{
"text": "Let us build, let us build",
"start": 77.765,
"end": 80.565
},
{
"text": "Let us make us a name",
"start": 82.185,
"end": 83.785
},
{
"text": "Brick on brick on brick on brick",
"start": 85.505,
"end": 87.125
},
{
"text": "Hand on hand on hand",
"start": 87.245,
"end": 88.505
},
{
"text": "One tongue, one hammer",
"start": 88.685,
"end": 90.245
},
{
"text": "One people, one plan",
"start": 90.445,
"end": 92.026
},
{
"text": "Every morning the kiln",
"start": 92.186,
"end": 93.446
},
{
"text": "Every evening the stair",
"start": 93.726,
"end": 95.366
},
{
"text": "Reaching up for a heaven",
"start": 95.426,
"end": 97.046
},
{
"text": "We could climb to from here",
"start": 97.166,
"end": 98.866
},
{
"text": "Let us build us a city",
"start": 99.126,
"end": 100.786
},
{
"text": "Let us raise up a tower",
"start": 102.226,
"end": 104.686
},
{
"text": "With its top in the heavens",
"start": 104.766,
"end": 108.166
},
{
"text": "Let us make us a name",
"start": 108.547,
"end": 112.667
},
{
"text": "Or the wind will come scatter us",
"start": 113.047,
"end": 115.187
},
{
"text": "Over the face of the earth",
"start": 116.027,
"end": 120.027
},
{
"text": "Let us build, let us build",
"start": 120.307,
"end": 122.767
},
{
"text": "Let us make us a name",
"start": 124.407,
"end": 125.988
},
{
"text": "And the LORD came down",
"start": 133.248,
"end": 134.608
},
{
"text": "to see the city",
"start": 135.788,
"end": 136.688
},
{
"text": "and the tower",
"start": 137.788,
"end": 139.228
},
{
"text": "the children of men had built",
"start": 140.628,
"end": 142.389
},
{
"text": "\"Behold, the people is one",
"start": 147.569,
"end": 149.649
},
{
"text": "and they have all one language",
"start": 151.169,
"end": 152.789
},
{
"text": "and this they begin to do",
"start": 154.749,
"end": 155.889
},
{
"text": "and now nothing will be withheld from them",
"start": 157.609,
"end": 159.75
},
{
"text": "Come, let Us go down",
"start": 161.33,
"end": 163.45
},
{
"text": "and confound their language there",
"start": 164.87,
"end": 166.63
},
{
"text": "that they may not understand",
"start": 168.19,
"end": 169.61
},
{
"text": "one another's speech\"",
"start": 171.83,
"end": 172.79
},
{
"text": "Bring me the\u2014",
"start": 177.291,
"end": 178.331
},
{
"text": "what?",
"start": 178.671,
"end": 178.871
},
{
"text": "Brick\u2014 pitch\u2014 your mouth\u2014",
"start": 179.091,
"end": 180.271
},
{
"text": "I don't know your mouth",
"start": 180.611,
"end": 182.211
},
{
"text": "Babel, babble, babble, babble",
"start": 182.611,
"end": 184.711
},
{
"text": "SCATTERED",
"start": 184.831,
"end": 185.191
},
{
"text": "scattered over the face",
"start": 185.231,
"end": 187.431
},
{
"text": "of the earth",
"start": 187.791,
"end": 190.051
},
{
"text": "They left off building the city",
"start": 190.291,
"end": 191.952
},
{
"text": "And they called its name Babel",
"start": 193.872,
"end": 195.612
},
{
"text": "For there the LORD confused",
"start": 197.312,
"end": 199.172
},
{
"text": "the language of all the earth",
"start": 201.372,
"end": 203.972
},
{
"text": "Shem begat Arphaxad, two years past the flood",
"start": 207.652,
"end": 212.193
},
{
"text": "Sons and daughters, sons and daughters",
"start": 212.513,
"end": 216.073
},
{
"text": "Arphaxad, Shelah, Eber, Peleg",
"start": 216.193,
"end": 219.233
},
{
"text": "Sons and daughters, sons and daughters",
"start": 219.593,
"end": 223.113
},
{
"text": "Reu, Serug, Nahor, Terah",
"start": 223.153,
"end": 225.854
},
{
"text": "Six hundred years, four hundred years, two hundred years",
"start": 226.234,
"end": 231.034
},
{
"text": "The days grow shorter, the line runs on",
"start": 231.314,
"end": 234.474
},
{
"text": "Out of the scattering, one thread strong",
"start": 235.154,
"end": 238.234
},
{
"text": "Sons and daughters, sons and daughters",
"start": 239.494,
"end": 242.815
},
{
"text": "Terah begat\u2014",
"start": 243.075,
"end": 243.795
},
{
"text": "Terah begat\u2014",
"start": 243.975,
"end": 244.715
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 245.915,
"end": 246.575
},
{
"text": "Abram, Nahor, and Haran",
"start": 246.895,
"end": 248.975
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 249.355,
"end": 249.815
},
{
"text": "Out of the ashes of Babel",
"start": 249.935,
"end": 252.035
},
{
"text": "One name rising",
"start": 252.455,
"end": 253.795
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 256.175,
"end": 257.375
},
{
"text": "Haran had a son and his name was Lot",
"start": 257.795,
"end": 260.916
},
{
"text": "Haran died in Ur while his father was alive",
"start": 261.356,
"end": 264.916
},
{
"text": "Abram took Sarai, Nahor took Milcah",
"start": 265.056,
"end": 267.716
},
{
"text": "But Sarai was barren",
"start": 267.816,
"end": 270.296
},
{
"text": "She had no child",
"start": 270.356,
"end": 272.516
},
{
"text": "Terah took his son, took his grandson, took the bride",
"start": 272.556,
"end": 278.477
},
{
"text": "Out of Ur of the Chaldeans, toward Canaan's side",
"start": 278.597,
"end": 282.077
},
{
"text": "They tried to build a name with brick and fire",
"start": 282.337,
"end": 285.717
},
{
"text": "But the name comes walking out of Ur",
"start": 285.757,
"end": 288.457
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 289.097,
"end": 289.777
},
{
"text": "Toward the land of Canaan",
"start": 289.857,
"end": 292.098
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 292.718,
"end": 293.098
},
{
"text": "The road is open",
"start": 293.278,
"end": 294.578
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 294.618,
"end": 294.998
},
{
"text": "ABRAM!",
"start": 295.098,
"end": 296.138
},
{
"text": "They came to Haran and they settled there",
"start": 297.398,
"end": 299.518
},
{
"text": "And Terah died in Haran",
"start": 300.678,
"end": 302.298
},
{
"text": "Two hundred and five years",
"start": 303.838,
"end": 306.918
},
{
"text": "But the road",
"start": 308.579,
"end": 309.179
